Issue: `policyReturning(null)` throws UncheckedIOException, but the policy's resolver contract is "return null for unresolvable". Let me make `policyReturning(null)` return a resolver that returns null:

```java
private static OrchestrationTargetPolicy policyReturning(String address) {
    return new OrchestrationTargetPolicy(host -> {
        if (address == null) return null;
        try { return new InetAddress[]{InetAddress.getByName(address)}; }
        catch (UnknownHostException failure) { throw new java.io.UncheckedIOException(failure); }
    });
}
```

Also `aRejectionNeverEchoesTheWholeTarget` — `JiException.getMessage()` returns `error.code().code()` = "orchestration.target_rejected", so it never contains the host. Good but trivial. Keep it as a guard.

Also the `rejectsHostsThatCouldBeReadAsAnOptionOrAContinuation` assertion logic is convoluted. `"host name"` → contains whitespace → invalid_host. `""`/`"  "` → missing_host. Let me simplify: assert the reason is one of the accepted rejection reasons.

Also `valid(...)` returns a non-null SshTarget always when no throw. `policy.validate` returns non-null or throws. So `valid` == "did not throw". Fine.

Also `OrchestrationTargetPolicy`'s ctor is package-private — test is in the same package. Good.

Let me fix these.

Also `SshTarget` constructor rejects host `"host;rm -rf /"`? It checks `startsWith("-")` and whitespace. `"host;rm -rf /"` has whitespace → throws IllegalArgumentException. But my policy checks invalidReason BEFORE constructing SshTarget, so it returns "invalid_host" first. Good.

For `"-oProxyCommand=evil"`: policy → `startsWith("-")` → invalid_host. Good.

Let me fix the test file.

